      "question": {
        ":question/id": "3fe83e25-a491-5f7c-b624-e2aecbbcfc65",
        ":question/problem": "Given that the distance from a point $P$ to the origin is $6,$ and that $P$ makes an angle of ${315}^{\u2218}$ with the positive $x$-axis, what are the Cartesian coordinates of $P?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We notice that the point $P$ is described using polar coordinates $(r,\\theta )$, where\n\n$$\nr=6,\\,\\theta ={315}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nTo convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta  \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{cos}\u2061({315}^{\u2218}) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta  \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{sin}\u2061({315}^{\u2218}) \\\\  & =6(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(3\\sqrt{2},-3\\sqrt{2}).$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "af20ccec-9741-587e-8b2c-0fb701159ee6",
