        ":question/problem": "Given that the distance from a point $P$ to the origin is $7,$ and that $P$ makes an angle of $0$ with the positive $x$-axis, what are the Cartesian coordinates of $P?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We notice that the point $P$ is described using polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ where\n\n$$\nr=7,\\,\\theta =0.\n$$\n\nTo convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta  \\\\ x & =7\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(0) \\\\ x & =7\\cdot 1 \\\\ x & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta  \\\\ y & =7\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(0) \\\\ y & =7\\cdot 0 \\\\ y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(7,0).$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
